It's amazing!

3
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,660
I know, isn't it?

4
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:32,220
Welcome to Arun.

5
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:33,977
It's the center of Alfheim.

6
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:36,397
It's also the biggest city in this world.

7
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:38,700
Yeah, we finally got here.

8
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:40,360
How exciting!

9
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,140
I've never been to a city
this big before. Me neither.

10
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:48,520
The ore light's so beautiful,
like a bunch of twinkling stars.

11
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:53,298
Attention, players.

12
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:57,940
The server will be down today,
January the Knight, from 4 a .m.

13
00:00:58,060 --> 00:00:58,960
to 3 p .m.

14
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,609
for scheduled maintenance.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,706
We ask that all players please log out
no later than 10 minutes before shutdown.

16
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:10,190
Phew.

17
00:01:10,273 --> 00:01:12,077
I guess that does it for us for today.

18
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:14,101
Let's go find an inn and log out.

19
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:16,050
Sure.

20
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:22,097
Well I hope we can find
someplace good nothing too pricey

21
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:25,457
though I sort of blew through
all my cash today and why's

22
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:28,037
that oh right you were showing
off and you gave all your

23
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:31,767
money to you should have saved
a little for the in big spender

24
00:01:33,700 --> 00:01:38,288
your dad's financially challenged do you
know if there's a cheap inn anywhere?

25
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:43,697
There's one there, and from what
I can tell, it's super cheap.

26
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,520
Great, super cheap, yay.

27
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,320
Come on, let's go.

28
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:49,360
Hey, wait for me!

29
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:38,057
I can't see the future!

30
00:02:38,140 --> 00:02:43,157
I can't see the future!

31
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:47,300
I'm still saying that
I'm still saying that.

32
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:49,217
I'm still saying that
I'm still in my heart.

33
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,597
I'm still seeing the

34
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:51,510
feeling of

35
00:02:51,593 --> 00:02:52,423
a

36
00:02:52,506 --> 00:02:57,720
sudden.

37
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,080
An opening.

38
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:24,660
Hey, Sugu. Good morning.

39
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,160
Morning, Kazutou.

40
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,887
Someone looked sleepy today.

41
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:34,441
When'd you get to bed last night?

42
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,430
I don't know.

43
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:38,380
Around four, I think? Whoa.

44
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,277
A kid like you shouldn't be up that late.

45
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:42,536
What were you doing?

46
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:45,840
Oh, uh, tooling around online?

47
00:04:48,040 --> 00:04:50,040
Just don't go too overboard, okay?

48
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:52,170
Right.

49
00:04:52,253 --> 00:04:53,460
Like I'm one to talk.

50
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:55,800
Hey, Sugou.

51
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:58,080
Turn around for a sec. Why?

52
00:04:58,340 --> 00:04:59,460
Go on, turn around.

53
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,270
Okay.

54
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:21,280
How far does this hallway go?

55
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:36,157
No way.

56
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,200
It's a map.

57
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,660
Where is it?

58
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:44,664
There's got to be a console
where I can log out.

59
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,820
Experiment hangar?

60
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:08,452
To make up for that water gag you pulled,

61
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:11,069
you owe me one green
tea raspberry parfait.

62
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:12,658
You cool with that?

63
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:14,130
Alright.

64
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:15,641
Then we're even.

65
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:18,962
We could go get him today
if you're not too busy.

66
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,200
I can't today.

67
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:23,557
I have to do something in the afternoon,

68
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,522
and I was also planning
on going to the hospital.

69
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,360
Oh, right.

70
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:35,640
Hey, I was wondering, is it okay
if I go with you to the hospital?

71
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,000
Sure, why not?

72
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:42,622
I'm sure it'll make Asuna happy.

73
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:47,961
Come on, let's eat, I'm starving.

74
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:18,137
Is that a...

75
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:21,691
Did you know that by expanding
the brain's control regions,

76
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:26,060
one could influence a person's
thoughts, emotions, and memories?

77
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:31,640
It's suffering!

78
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,797
They're all...

79
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:36,900
players.

80
00:07:41,840 --> 00:07:43,157
Oh, my God.

81
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:44,580
This is horrible.

82
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,500
He won't get away with this.

83
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,180
Not if I can do anything about it.

84
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,900
Don't worry. It'll be okay.

85
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:00,638
I'm gonna save you.

86
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,580
Time to see what everyone's up to.

87
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,400
Ooh, this guy's dreaming
about Spica again.

88
00:08:09,960 --> 00:08:13,300
His B-13 and B-14 fields
are way off the scale.

89
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,517
Look, his 16's getting up there, too.

90
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,857
He's really excited.

91
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,800
It's only the third experiment.

92
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:20,691
Maybe it's a coincidence.

93
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,624
No, it's definitely the
induced emotion circuit.

94
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:25,837
He's over the threshold now because of the

95
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:28,508
frequency at which the
imagery is occurring.

96
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,030
Hmm.

97
00:08:30,113 --> 00:08:31,417
Then we have to keep monitoring him.

98
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:32,971
I'll put him on the list.

99
00:08:33,120 --> 00:08:36,120
Hey, I was wondering, what's
happening with school?

100
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:37,360
What about it?

101
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:40,177
It's just that you were supposed
to start high school last year,

102
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:42,557
and it'd suck if you got too far behind.

103
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:44,620
Yeah, well, I don't know.

104
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:48,417
They said something about me
having to go to school in the city.

105
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:51,737
It's kind of a temporary thing
they set up in an old building.

106
00:08:51,820 --> 00:08:54,996
Middle schoolers, high
schoolers, everyone's from SAO.

107
00:08:55,080 --> 00:08:56,120
Now departing.

108
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:58,637
You can get in without taking a test.

109
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:02,077
And once you graduate, you can
take the college entrance exams.

110
00:09:02,160 --> 00:09:02,990
Really?

111
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,280
If you ask me, that's a pretty good deal.

112
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:10,938
But it sucks they're cramming
you together like that.

113
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:13,708
I get why they're doing it.

114
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:14,957
When you think about it,

115
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:18,177
we were all trapped inside that
death game for more than two years.

116
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:21,297
So no one knows what that
experience did to our minds.

117
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,615
This is how they'll keep an eye on us.

118
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,650
Seriously?

119
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:28,817
If I wanted to get into a normal high
school now, it'd be way too hard.

120
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,977
I'd have to spend a whole
year in cram school,

121
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:33,757
but then I'd basically be
starting over from scratch.

122
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:38,664
I could always just take the exams now and
see what happens, but I doubt I'd pass.

123
00:09:38,800 --> 00:09:39,657
What are you saying?

124
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,857
You'd totally pass.

125
00:09:40,940 --> 00:09:44,822
You're smart and you've got good
grades my grades used to be good.

126
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,717
I haven't studied for two years.

127
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:47,630
Remember?

128
00:09:47,713 --> 00:09:48,974
I've got a great idea.

129
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,260
I can be your tutor. Oh sweet.

130
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:54,833
Then you can help me with math
and information technology

131
00:10:08,100 --> 00:10:09,000
There it is

132
00:10:11,980 --> 00:10:13,980
The system console.

133
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,320
They didn't see me.

134
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:19,730
Good.

135
00:10:28,780 --> 00:10:30,160
Please work.

136
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,100
This is it!

137
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:52,990
Wow!

138
00:10:53,073 --> 00:10:54,220
That's a big hospital!

139
00:10:54,600 --> 00:10:57,020
The inside's amazing, too. Like a hotel.

140
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:18,060
Asuna Yuki.

141
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:21,440
She used her real-life
name for her avatar.

142
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:24,457
That's not something a lot of people do.

143
00:11:24,540 --> 00:11:26,305
I can't believe you know that.

144
00:11:27,420 --> 00:11:31,302
Asuna's the only person I ever met
who played under her real name.

145
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:36,838
I'll introduce you.

146
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,460
This is Asuna.

147
00:11:38,880 --> 00:11:40,857
Knights of the Blood
Oath, second in Kameha.

148
00:11:40,940 --> 00:11:42,705
They call her Lightning Flash.

149
00:11:43,040 --> 00:11:47,240
I can never match her speed in battle
or her accuracy with the sword.

150
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:50,820
Asuna, this is my sister, Suguha.

151
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,160
Hello, Asuna.

152
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:55,560
Nice to meet you.

153
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,980
Who are you?

154
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:09,769
You want to tell us
what you're doing here?

155
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:14,000
Hey, let go of me.

156
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,437
Zuko's a very good friend of mine.

157
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:20,817
I have his permission to be here and was
just about to leave when you grabbed me.

158
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:23,665
No one told me you were
going to be here today.

159
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:25,853
Did you know about her?

160
00:12:26,040 --> 00:12:26,940
Uh, no.

161
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:31,417
All I know is that he doesn't want
anyone seeing this stuff ever.

162
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:32,330
Hmm.

163
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:33,920
Hang on a sec.

164
00:12:34,220 --> 00:12:35,300
This is the girl.

165
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:38,917
You know the one Sugou keeps locked
up at the top of the world tree?

166
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:39,977
Right, right.

167
00:12:40,060 --> 00:12:41,700
I heard about her.

168
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:47,480
I don't think it's fair how the boss gets
to have all the fun with this cute girl.

169
00:12:48,820 --> 00:12:49,920
Oh, come on.

170
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,860
Stop struggling. Stop it!

171
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:53,800
Let me go, you monster!

172
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:56,400
Oh, don't be so mean.

173
00:12:56,720 --> 00:13:00,308
After all, you interrupted our
deep sense mapping experiment.

174
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:02,617
You're supposed to be scientists, right?

175
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:04,440
All this? It's wrong.

176
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:07,052
It's illegal to mess with people's minds.

177
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:08,580
Illegal and unethical.

178
00:13:09,240 --> 00:13:10,070
Well,

179
00:13:10,153 --> 00:13:11,877
it's more ethical than sticking electrical

180
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:14,237
probes into the brain of some poor animal,

181
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,320
wouldn't you say?

182
00:13:15,580 --> 00:13:18,840
Our experiments are
just dreams, that's all.

183
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:20,790
He's right.

184
00:13:20,873 --> 00:13:23,297
Sometimes we show them
the most wonderful dreams.

185
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,497
Dreams you wish you'd never wake up from.

186
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,051
I wish I could have that.

187
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,960
You're insane.

188
00:13:30,780 --> 00:13:32,980
The boss is out on business, right?

189
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:35,737
Log out and go see what he
wants us to do with her.

190
00:13:35,820 --> 00:13:38,880
Oh, fine, whatever. Listen, though.

191
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:42,057
Until I get back, don't
do anything I wouldn't do.

192
00:13:42,140 --> 00:13:43,022
Oh, yeah, sure.

193
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,553
Hurry up and get going.

194
00:13:49,900 --> 00:13:51,420
You can't keep me here!

195
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:52,980
Put me down right now!

196
00:13:53,160 --> 00:13:54,520
I'm sorry, but I can't.

197
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,797
The boss would kill me if I let you go.

198
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,120
Oh, wait, I have it.

199
00:13:58,280 --> 00:14:00,417
Why don't you and I take electro drugs?

200
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:04,676
I'm so bored with dolls, but you look
like someone I can have fun with.

201
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:09,220
Stop it!

202
00:14:10,240 --> 00:14:11,070
No!

203
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:14,610
Stop!

204
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:23,410
Okay!

205
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:25,017
I'm putting you down!

206
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,688
Here's me putting you down!

207
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:28,470
Jeez!

208
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:31,978
Next time I'll remember to
turn my paint sensors off!

209
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:36,300
Okay, what happened here? Hmm? What?

210
00:14:37,120 --> 00:14:37,950
Nothing.

211
00:14:38,033 --> 00:14:38,863
Nothing happened.

212
00:14:38,946 --> 00:14:39,776
So, what'd the boss say?

213
00:14:39,859 --> 00:14:41,120
Oh, he was so pissed.

214
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:43,637
He said we had to put her
back in the cage upstairs,

215
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:46,602
change the passcode, and
keep an eye on her 24-7.

216
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,917
I was just about to have some fun.

217
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,294
Okay, I say we walk her back
instead of Teleport her.

218
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:56,440
I want to enjoy this
feeling as long as I can.

219
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,394
You know what I think?

220
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,580
You're a perv.

221
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,301
Stop struggling.

222
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,951
It won't do you any good.

223
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,700
Let me go!

224
00:15:10,140 --> 00:15:11,380
She's really pretty.

225
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:15,401
I feel sorry for her that
she hasn't woken up yet.

226
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:22,062
I don't know if coming
here was such a good idea.

227
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:24,880
I'm so confused.

228
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,820
I don't know how I feel.

229
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:31,211
I thought if I met her, I'd figure it out.

230
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:35,180
But now, I don't know what I want.

231
00:15:35,820 --> 00:15:37,680
Do I want to be a good sister?

232
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:42,520
Or... what?

233
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:01,970
Kazutou...

234
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:09,300
Hmm don't go anywhere.

235
00:16:09,520 --> 00:16:11,932
I hope we have another chance to hang out

236
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,157
This won't stop me Kirito. No way.

237
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,497
I'll never give up.

238
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:26,580
I'll find a way to get out of here

239
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:44,260
Hey, Leafa.

240
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,080
What's wrong? You okay?

241
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:53,930
Uh-uh.

242
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:55,820
I'm not okay at all.

243
00:16:56,320 --> 00:16:57,797
I just...

244
00:16:57,880 --> 00:16:59,057
I just...

245
00:16:59,140 --> 00:17:01,260
I just got my heart broken.

246
00:17:05,880 --> 00:17:07,340
I-I'm sorry.

247
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:09,717
I don't know why I'm telling you this.

248
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,760
We just met.

249
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:16,260
And I know it's not cool for players to
drag their real-life problems into the game.

250
00:17:17,200 --> 00:17:18,460
It's okay to cry.

251
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:21,840
Doesn't matter if you're
here or in the real world.

252
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:23,477
There's no rule.

253
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:26,795
Even in a game, you can show
your feelings if you want.

254
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:29,530
Kirito?

255
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:39,800
I'm in love with my brother, and that's
something I can't tell anyone about, ever.

256
00:17:41,520 --> 00:17:44,700
I have to bury these
feelings deep in my heart.

257
00:17:45,480 --> 00:17:48,840
Maybe then, someday, I can forget.

258
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,420
I'm okay now.

259
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,382
Thanks for the pep talk, Kirito.

260
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:07,319
You're really sweet, you know that?

261
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:11,517
Yeah, well, you're probably the only
person who thinks that about me.

262
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:13,365
You want to log off for today?

263
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,952
I can make it the rest of the way myself.

264
00:18:16,480 --> 00:18:20,520
No, I mean, I've come this far,
so I might as well go all the way.

265
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,160
Come on, let's go.

266
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,120
Yui, you here?

267
00:18:39,340 --> 00:18:40,180
Good morning.

268
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:42,128
I hope you both slept well.

269
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:43,720
Good morning, Yui.

270
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,130
Hey,

271
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:50,057
I didn't get the chance to ask you yesterday,
but, like, do NaviPixies ever sleep?

272
00:18:50,140 --> 00:18:50,970
Oh, no.

273
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:53,517
See, whenever Daddy logs out of the game,

274
00:18:53,600 --> 00:18:57,377
I shut down my input circuits and
process the data I've acquired.

275
00:18:57,460 --> 00:19:00,897
You could consider it a little
like human sleep, but it's not.

276
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,700
Then how come you yawned?

277
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:06,757
Oh, well, that's what humans do
during their boot-up sequence.

278
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,917
When Daddy yawns, it usually
lasts for eight seconds.

279
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,412
Please keep the weird trivia to yourself.

280
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,120
You ready to go? Yep.

281
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:21,740
There's tons of people here.

282
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:24,609
I guess it really is
the center of Alfheim.

283
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:28,220
It seems all the ferry races
the world over are here.

284
00:19:28,460 --> 00:19:30,519
Look how they're all getting along.

285
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,900
They flew right off!

286
00:19:50,820 --> 00:19:53,460
There it is, the World Tree.

287
00:19:57,720 --> 00:20:01,220
Yeah, and it looks even more
amazing up close, doesn't it?

288
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:05,480
Um, I heard there's supposed to
be a city up there at the top.

289
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:06,760
What else?

290
00:20:07,860 --> 00:20:12,177
Oberon the Fairy King lives there, along
with the Alf, the Fairies of Light.

291
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:17,084
And they say the first race to get to the
top and see the king will be coming out.

292
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,497
Has anyone ever tried climbing
up the side of that thing?

293
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:22,997
They made the whole perimeter
of the trunk off limits,

294
00:20:23,080 --> 00:20:25,845
so a player can't even
get close enough to try.

295
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,797
And if you just fly straight up,

296
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:31,717
the flight limit of your wings would
expire before you even got halfway.

297
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,976
I heard about some players who tried.

298
00:20:34,080 --> 00:20:37,517
They got more than halfway up
by piggybacking on each other.

299
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:39,457
Yeah, I heard about them, all right.

300
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:43,117
But they could only make it up to
the lowest branches before bailing.

301
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:47,141
The GMs freaked out and fixed it,
so no one could ever do it again.

302
00:20:47,540 --> 00:20:48,417
Know what they did?

303
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:51,441
They put a barrier up there
just above the clouds.

304
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:52,790
Interesting.

305
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:54,161
All right, then.

306
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:56,137
Let's head to the base of the trunk.

307
00:20:56,220 --> 00:20:57,280
Right behind you.

308
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:20,217
Once we pass through that gate,
we're in the world's heart.

309
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,241
The central district of our room.

310
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:32,770
What, Yui?

311
00:21:33,040 --> 00:21:34,158
Is something wrong?

312
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,230
Mommy!

313
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:40,560
It's Mommy! She's here!

314
00:21:42,980 --> 00:21:43,810
Are you sure?

315
00:21:43,893 --> 00:21:45,597
Yes, I'm positive! Hey, I...

316
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:48,268
I scanned again, and
it's Mommy's player ID!

317
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:51,360
Her coordinates are above us in the tree!

318
00:21:56,060 --> 00:21:56,890
Kirito!

319
00:21:58,300 --> 00:21:59,130
Wait!

320
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:00,990
Kirito!

321
00:22:02,380 --> 00:22:03,210
Kirito!

322
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:38,200
Next time, the grand quest.
